Task 1 - System Identification
FIELD	ANSWER
Proposed system title	Laundry Booking and Management System
Organization / environment	A neighborhood laundry shop in Impalambong, Malaybalay City, Bukidnon, serving students, working professionals, and families in the community.
System description	A web and mobile application backed by a relational database. Customers register, choose a laundry service, book a drop-off time slot at the shop, track their order status, pay, and give feedback. Staff process orders and record payments, and the administrator manages services, time slots, users, and reports. The system covers booking and shop management only (no delivery).
Existing process	Customers book by walking in, calling, or messaging through social media or text. Staff write orders on paper receipts or notebooks, compute prices by hand based on weight and service type, and tell customers the status of their laundry only when asked. Payments, claim stubs, and customer records are kept in physical logbooks or loosely organized spreadsheets.
Problems encountered	Orders are lost, mixed up, or delayed; customers cannot tell when laundry is ready; pricing errors and unrecorded payments reduce income; owners cannot easily monitor workload, staff performance, or revenue; peak hours cause long queues while idle hours go unused because there is no scheduling.
Why the system is necessary	A centralized database replaces scattered paper and spreadsheet records with accurate, searchable, and secure data. Online booking with slot limits balances workload, real-time tracking reduces repeated inquiries, automatic computation removes pricing errors, and reports help the owner make decisions.

