Task 6 - DBMS Selection
ITEM	ANSWER
Database name and classification	MySQL (MariaDB distribution bundled with XAMPP) - Relational (SQL) DBMS
Justification	The data is structured and highly relational (users, orders, slots, payments), so it needs foreign keys, constraints, and ACID transactions to keep bookings and payments consistent.
MySQL/MariaDB is free, runs locally through XAMPP, and works well with the REST API backend serving both the web and mobile apps.
Advantages	Free and open source; strong support for foreign keys, indexes, transactions, and role-based user privileges; large community and documentation; easy local setup and administration; good driver support for the backend.
Limitations	Horizontal scaling is harder than with some NoSQL systems; schema changes need careful planning; the default XAMPP setup is not secure (root without password) and must be hardened; fewer advanced features than PostgreSQL.
Management and modeling tools	phpMyAdmin (administration), XAMPP (local server), MySQL Workbench or dbdiagram.io (ERD design, from Day 3), Git/GitHub (version control), VS Code (editing).



